sequenceDiagram
  %% status: draft
  %% command: tool:converge
  %% kind: tool.converge
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP
  participant GW as Gateway
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>control Node
  participant N as Target Node
  CLI->>GW: tool:converge --node=ID
  %%> Command:
  %%> - syntax: `--node=ID [--tool-id=TOOL ...] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  Note over GW: Admit registered Tools<br/>with desired coordinates
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the Node is active and SSH-managed on Linux or macOS
  %%> - the caller has access to the Node and no competing write owns a selected manager on this Node
  %%> - admit all eligible Tools, or only the selected memberships, and the apt repositories they reference; one on another repository's URI and suite is refused
  alt no registered Tools
    GW-->>CLI: Complete · changed 0
  else registered Tools
    GW->>SW: Start Tools-only Operation
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted
    SW->>N: Publish apt repositories<br/>over pinned SSH
    %%> Repositories:
    %%> - each one is that repository's own add: hold its preferences to its owned Tools, verify the key, write keyring and source, read its index
    %%> - its outcome makes it ready or failed; a failed one stops only its own Tools
    SW->>N: Reconcile Tools<br/>over pinned SSH
    %%> Result:
    %%> - install missing packages and apply exact desired versions; leave existing unpinned packages alone
    %%> - do not run core, role, network, or host Conn phases
    %%> - add a Tool to its repository's preference only after it is verified installed
    SW-->>GW: Report changes, versions<br/>and repository outcomes
    CLI->>GW: Follow the Operation
    GW-->>CLI: Terminal receipt
  end
